<title>UK: UPS unions call off Brussels meeting.</title>
<headline>UPS unions call off Brussels meeting.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A meeting to be held in Brussels on Thursday of representatives of unionised employees of United Parcel Service has been called off following the settlement of the Teamsters union's dispute with UPS in the U.S., a spokesman for the International Transport Workers Federation (ITF) here said.</p>
<p>The ITF-UPS World Council was set up in February this year by unions as a global body to coordinate their dealings with UPS and had planned to meet on Thursday to co-ordinate action against UPS.</p>
<p>A Teamsters delegation which came to Europe to lobby European unions to support their dispute against UPS is still in Europe. - Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
